@node Gowl AI Field Usage
@section Using it

@enumerate
@item
Put the keyboard in a text field in any window.  Select part of the
text if you only want that part changed.
@item
Press @kbd{Super+Ctrl+a}.  The compositor's menu card lists the
actions, titled with what they will act on (``AI on the selection'',
``AI on this field'').
@item
Pick one.  A toast on the bar says what is running and on how much
text.
@item
The answer replaces the text.  A toast says it is done.
@end enumerate

@table @code
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field
Choose an action for the focused field; while one runs, offer to cancel
it.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-proofread
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-proofread
Fix spelling and grammar, changing nothing else.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-rewrite
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-rewrite
Rewrite: clearer and tighter.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-shorten
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-shorten
Shorten, keeping the facts and the voice.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-translate
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-translate
Translate into @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-translate-language}.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-custom
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-custom
Rewrite as an instruction you type says.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-run
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-run
Run any action of @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-actions} by name.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-undo
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-undo
Put back the text the last action replaced.
@findex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel
Cancel the action in progress.
@end table

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-action-keys
All of them return at once.  The direct commands skip the menu; give
them keys with @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-action-keys}:

@lisp
(setq cmacs-gowl-ai-field-action-keys
      '(("Super+Ctrl+g" . proofread)
        ("Super+Ctrl+s" . shorten)))
@end lisp

@subheading The chooser

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-chooser
The list is drawn by gowl's menu card (the @samp{menu} module's
@samp{menu-choose} command), so it appears over the application and
typing filters it, exactly as @kbd{Super+space} does.  No Emacs frame
is involved.  When the card is not available---the menu module is not
loaded---or @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-chooser} is @code{minibuffer},
the choice is read with @code{completing-read} in a small floating
minibuffer-only frame instead.

The same frame is where a free-form instruction is typed (``Custom
instruction...''): the menu card can pick a row but cannot take a
sentence.  That read occupies Emacs's thread, as the gowl menu's does,
and not the compositor's.  When it is over the keyboard is handed back
to the window it came from.

When there is an edit to undo in the focused window, the list ends with
an @samp{Undo: ...} row.

@subheading Progress and cancelling

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-progress-interval
@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-timeout
@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel-key
One action runs at a time.  A toast is shown when the model is asked,
every @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-progress-interval} seconds while it
answers (with how many characters have arrived), and at the end.
Pressing @kbd{Super+Ctrl+a} while an action is running offers
@samp{Cancel: ...} and @samp{Let it finish} instead of the actions;
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel} (and
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel-key}, unset by default) cancels with
no menu.  A cancelled action stops the model request, lets go of the
field and types nothing.  A model that has not answered after
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-timeout} seconds (120) is given up on the
same way.

@subheading Undo

The text as it was read is kept.  @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-undo} puts
it back, on two conditions: the window the edit was made in holds the
keyboard, and its field still holds exactly the answer.  A field edited
since is not overwritten---the old text goes to the kill ring and a
toast says so.  The application's own undo works as well, since it saw
one edit.

Only the last edit is kept, and only for this Emacs session.

@node Gowl AI Field Scope
@section What is acted on

The field is read the way the editor reads it (@pxref{Gowl Edit
Field}), by the same code.

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{A selection}, when the application reports one over
text-input-v3: only the selected text is sent, and only it is replaced.
@item
@strong{The whole text the application reported}, otherwise.
@item
@strong{A window around the cursor}, when the field is longer than the
protocol can carry (about 4000 bytes).  Only that window is rewritten,
and the toast says ``the text around the cursor''.  With
@code{cmacs-gowl-edit-field-partial-action} set to @code{fallback} the
whole field is fetched through the clipboard instead.
@item
@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-clipboard-fallback
@strong{The whole field, through the clipboard fallback}, for a window
with no text input (X11 programs, some toolkits).  A selection cannot
be learnt that way.  The fallback and its deny list are the editor's
(@code{cmacs-gowl-edit-field-fallback},
@code{cmacs-gowl-edit-field-fallback-deny}---never a terminal);
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-clipboard-fallback} set to @code{nil} turns
it off for AI actions only.
@end itemize

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-max-chars
Text that is empty, longer than @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-max-chars}
(20000), or longer than @code{cmacs-ai-target-max-chars} is refused: a
rewrite of clipped text would be written back over the whole.

@node Gowl AI Field Writing
@section Writing the answer back

When the answer is complete:

@enumerate
@item
A code fence or a pair of quotes the model put around it against orders
is removed (@code{cmacs-ai-proofread--strip-wrapping}, as the in-place
proofreader does).
@item
The focused window is compared with the one that was read.  If it is
another, the answer is put on the kill ring and nothing is typed.
@item
The field is read again (@code{cmacs-gowl-edit-field-verify}).  If its
text is not what was read, the answer is put on the kill ring and
nothing is typed.
@item
One edit is sent: ``delete these bytes around the cursor, insert
this'', the smallest that turns the old text into the new.
@end enumerate

The kill ring is also where the answer goes when the application does
not take the edit, or the window was closed while the model was
working.

@node Gowl AI Field Actions
@section Actions and prompts

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-actions
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-actions} is an alist of @code{(@var{name}
. @var{plist})}, in menu order.

@table @code
@item :label
The menu row.
@item :op
The cmacs-ai text operation that supplies the prompts: @code{proofread}
or @code{rephrase}.
@item :how
How to do it: a string, or a function returning one.  Omitted, the
operation's own default.
@item :ask
Non-@code{nil} reads @code{:how} from the user when the action is
chosen.
@item :system
A system prompt of your own instead of the operation's.
@end table

The prompts are not copies.  An action names an operation in
@code{cmacs-ai-textops--specs}, and its system prompt is read through
that operation's variable when the action runs---
@code{cmacs-ai-proofread-system-prompt},
@code{cmacs-ai-rephrase-system-prompt}---so customising those for the
region commands changes a text field's answers too.  The user message
is built by the same function the region commands use.

The shipped actions: @code{proofread}, @code{rewrite}, @code{shorten},
@code{formal}, @code{friendly}, @code{translate}, @code{custom}.
Adding one:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'cmacs-gowl-ai-field-actions
             '(bullets :label "As a bullet list" :op rephrase
                       :how "Turn it into a short bullet list.")
             t)
@end lisp

Whatever the model answers replaces the text, so a @code{:system} of
your own must make it answer with the new text and nothing else.

@subheading Provider and model

@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-provider
@vindex cmacs-gowl-ai-field-model
By default field actions use what the region text commands use:
@code{cmacs-ai-textops-provider} and @code{cmacs-ai-textops-model}
(and, where those are @code{nil}, @code{cmacs-ai-default-provider} and
@code{cmacs-ai-default-model}).  @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-provider}
overrides the provider for this feature alone;
@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-model} then goes with it, and @code{nil}
means that provider's default rather than a model inherited from
another provider.

@node Gowl AI Field Privacy
@section Privacy

@cindex redaction, text fields
The text of the field is sent to the configured model.  That cannot be
otherwise, and the user asked for it by name.

@strong{The field's text is not passed through
@code{cmacs-redact-text}.}  This is deliberate.  The redaction rules
exist to keep what the user did @emph{not} offer away from a model;
here the user pointed at this text and asked for it to be rewritten.
Redacting it would also be destructive: the model would rewrite a text
with holes punched in it, and that would be written back over the
original.

What is honoured, before anything is read:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{The edit-field deny list}, @code{cmacs-gowl-edit-field-deny}:
password managers, password prompts, the lock screen.
@item
@strong{The redaction rule set, asked about the window.}
@code{cmacs-redact-window} is called with the focused window's app-id,
title and pid.  A window the rules exclude is refused.  So is every
window when the rules have failed to load, or the redaction library
cannot be loaded at all: this fails closed.
@item
@strong{Password fields.}  A field its application marks as a password
or PIN (content purpose 8 or 9, or the hidden-text or sensitive-data
hint) is refused once read, and never reaches the model or the
clipboard fallback.
@end itemize

Nothing but the field's text and the instruction reaches the model: not
the window's title, not its application.

One limit to know: through the clipboard fallback an application cannot
say that a field is a password field.  Applications do not copy out of
those, but set @code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-clipboard-fallback} to
@code{nil} if the model should only ever see text an application
described over text-input.

@node Gowl AI Field Options
@section Options

@table @code
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-key
Compositor key of the chooser (@code{"Super+Ctrl+a"}); @code{nil} for
none.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-undo-key
Compositor key of the undo (@code{nil}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-cancel-key
Compositor key of the cancel (@code{nil}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-action-keys
Alist of @code{(@var{key} . @var{action})} run with no menu
(@code{nil}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-actions
The actions, in menu order (seven of them).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-translate-language
What @code{translate} translates into (@code{"English"}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-provider
Provider for this feature; @code{nil} means the text commands'.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-model
Model for this feature (@code{nil}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-chooser
@code{card} (the menu card, the default) or @code{minibuffer}.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-clipboard-fallback
Whether the editor's clipboard fallback may be used (@code{t}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-max-chars
Longest text sent to a model (20000).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-timeout
Seconds to wait for the model (120); @code{nil} for no limit.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-progress-interval
Seconds between progress toasts (5); @code{nil} for none.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-toast
Report on the gowl bar as well as in the echo area (@code{t}).
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-prompt-frame-name
Title of the minibuffer frame (@code{"cmacs-ai-field-prompt"}); a float
rule matches it.
@item cmacs-gowl-ai-field-prompt-frame-width
Its width in columns (80).
@end table

@code{cmacs-gowl-ai-field-setup} unbinds the keys it bound last time
before binding, so a key taken out of an option stops working on the
next call.

The deny lists, the fallback, the partial-read policy and the
verify-before-write are the editor's options (@pxref{Gowl Edit Field}).

@node Gowl AI Field Sessions
@section For other features: headless edit-field sessions

@cindex headless session, edit field
Reaching a field is @file{cmacs-gowl-edit-field.el}'s business and
stays there.  To make that possible it gained @dfn{headless sessions}:
a session with a handler instead of an editor frame.  Any feature that
needs to read or replace a foreign text field should use these rather
than the C primitives, and so inherit the deny lists, the password
refusal, the fallback and the verify.

@defun cmacs-gowl-edit-field-focused-target
Return a plist describing the focused window: @code{:client},
@code{:id}, @code{:app-id}, @code{:title}, @code{:pid}, and
@code{:refused @var{why}} when its fields may not be touched.
@end defun

@defun cmacs-gowl-edit-field-read-async handler &optional target no-fallback
Read the focused field with no editor and return the session.
@end defun

@defun cmacs-gowl-edit-field-write-async session new
Replace what @var{session} read with @var{new}.  Does not move focus.
@end defun

@defun cmacs-gowl-edit-field-release session
Let go of @var{session} without writing.
@end defun

@defun cmacs-gowl-edit-field-session-info session
Return @code{:id}, @code{:app-id}, @code{:title}, @code{:method},
@code{:text} and @code{:complete} of @var{session}.
@end defun

The handler is called as:

@table @code
@item (@var{handler} 'read @var{session} @var{text} @var{cursor} @var{anchor})
The text is here.  @var{cursor} and @var{anchor} are character indexes;
they differ for a selection.  The session stays open.
@item (@var{handler} 'committed @var{session})
The new text is in the field.
@item (@var{handler} 'unchanged @var{session})
The new text was what the field held.
@item (@var{handler} 'failed @var{session} @var{why})
The read or the write did not happen; @var{why} is a sentence for the
user.
@end table

After any event but @code{read} the session is closed already.  A
headless session never moves the keyboard.  The editor command itself
is unchanged; a window whose field a headless session holds answers the
editor key with a message, and the other way round.

@node Gowl AI Field Limitations
@section Limitations

@itemize @bullet
@item
One action at a time, and one level of undo.
@item
The answer is the model's: a ``rewrite'' can change what the text says.
The undo, and the application's own, are one key away.
@item
A field longer than text-input carries is rewritten a window at a time
unless the clipboard fallback is used for it.
@item
Through the clipboard fallback the write is ``select all, paste'':
whether the application pasted cannot be known, so ``done'' there means
``sent''.
@item
Typing a free-form instruction needs an Emacs frame for the moment it
takes.
@item
The redaction check is of the @emph{window}.  Text in the field is sent
as it is, on purpose.
@end itemize

